   "id": "shabbat.104b.3",
   "daf": "104b",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ דְּיוֹ — דְּיוֹתָא. סַם — סַמָּא. סִקְרָא — אָמַר רַבָּה בַּר בַּר חָנָה: סְקַרְתָּא שְׁמָהּ. קוֹמוֹס — קוֹמָא. קַנְקַנְתּוֹם — אָמַר רַבָּה בַּר בַּר חָנָה אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: חַרְתָּא דְאוּשְׁכָּפֵי.",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» The Gemara defines the terms used in the mishna. «Deyo» is «deyota» made from soot. «Sam» is «samma,» which is yellow-tinged arsenic. «Sikra, Rabba bar bar Ḥana said: It is called sikreta» in Aramaic and is a lead-based red paint. «Komos» is «koma» in Aramaic, and it is an ink made with gum Arabic from the sap of a tree. «Kankantom, Rabba bar bar Ḥana said» that «Shmuel said:» This is «the black» substance «used by cobblers,» copper sulfate."
  }
 ],
